{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825511580,"sessionID":"ses_f461eb89fffeglVev82zxa58vo","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e9e872001Ute0p9V0pVrxFG","sessionID":"ses_f461eb89fffeglVev82zxa58vo","messageID":"msg_0b9e9d825001EPCyRN8mnzVaFD","type":"tool","id":"call_00_nrVNoyez9FLfXfQZkqYI7425","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/build.py","oldString":" ['Account', \"\\\"PetSmart's board began reviewing alternatives in early 2014 and, after JANA Partners disclosed a 9.9% stake on July 3, 2014 and Longview publicly urged a sale, decided on August 13 to explore a sale and announced it on August 19. A private strategic suitor, Industry Participant, re-approached J.P. Morgan on August 7 but was told it would not be invited, because of antitrust-timing risk. During mid-August to end-October J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants (three strategic, 24 financial); 15 financial buyers signed confidentiality and standstill agreements in the first week of October, received diligence and management presentations, and submitted one of six non-binding indications of interest due October 30. On November 3 the board advanced the four bidders at or above $80.00 to the final round; two of them combined as Bidder 3, which then valued the company at or below the market price and submitted nothing. Buyer Group bid $80.70 and Bidder 2 $80.35 on December 10; after the committee demanded improvement, their best-and-final bids on December 12 were $83.00 and $81.50, and the board approved the Buyer Group deal on December 13. The parties executed on December 14, 2014: $83.00 per share in cash, with Longview rolling 3,012,050 shares (~$250 million) into the buyer and no strategic acquirer reaching the final round.\\\"\"],","newString":" ['Account', \"PetSmart's board began reviewing alternatives in early 2014 and, after JANA Partners disclosed a 9.9% stake on July 3, 2014 and Longview publicly urged a sale, decided on August 13 to explore a sale and announced it on August 19. A private strategic suitor, Industry Participant, re-approached J.P. Morgan on August 7 but was told it would not be invited, because of antitrust-timing risk. During mid-August to end-October J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants (three strategic, 24 financial); 15 financial buyers signed confidentiality and standstill agreements in the first week of October, received diligence and management presentations, and submitted one of six non-binding indications of interest due October 30. On November 3 the board advanced the four bidders at or above $80.00 to the final round; two of them combined as Bidder 3, which then valued the company at or below the market price and submitted nothing. Buyer Group bid $80.70 and Bidder 2 $80.35 on December 10; after the committee demanded improvement, their best-and-final bids on December 12 were $83.00 and $81.50, and the board approved the Buyer Group deal on December 13. The parties executed on December 14, 2014: $83.00 per share in cash, with Longview rolling 3,012,050 shares (~$250 million) into the buyer and no strategic acquirer reaching the final round.\"],"},"output":"Edited /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build.py (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/build.py","patch":"Index: /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build.py\n===================================================================\n--- /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build.py\n+++ /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build.py\n@@ -418,9 +418,9 @@\n  ['Whole-company bids', 'Yes — all indications and bids were for the whole company (e.g., Buyer Group $83.00 per share in cash).'],\n  ['Currency and units of bid prices', 'US dollars, per share of common stock (all bids were cash; October indications did not state form).'],\n  ['Target financial advisers', 'J.P. Morgan Securities LLC (sole financial advisor; engagement letter effective 08/21/2014).'],\n  ['Target legal advisers', 'Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz.'],\n- ['Account', \"\\\"PetSmart's board began reviewing alternatives in early 2014 and, after JANA Partners disclosed a 9.9% stake on July 3, 2014 and Longview publicly urged a sale, decided on August 13 to explore a sale and announced it on August 19. A private strategic suitor, Industry Participant, re-approached J.P. Morgan on August 7 but was told it would not be invited, because of antitrust-timing risk. During mid-August to end-October J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants (three strategic, 24 financial); 15 financial buyers signed confidentiality and standstill agreements in the first week of October, received diligence and management presentations, and submitted one of six non-binding indications of interest due October 30. On November 3 the board advanced the four bidders at or above $80.00 to the final round; two of them combined as Bidder 3, which then valued the company at or below the market price and submitted nothing. Buyer Group bid $80.70 and Bidder 2 $80.35 on December 10; after the committee demanded improvement, their best-and-final bids on December 12 were $83.00 and $81.50, and the board approved the Buyer Group deal on December 13. The parties executed on December 14, 2014: $83.00 per share in cash, with Longview rolling 3,012,050 shares (~$250 million) into the buyer and no strategic acquirer reaching the final round.\\\"\"],\n+ ['Account', \"PetSmart's board began reviewing alternatives in early 2014 and, after JANA Partners disclosed a 9.9% stake on July 3, 2014 and Longview publicly urged a sale, decided on August 13 to explore a sale and announced it on August 19. A private strategic suitor, Industry Participant, re-approached J.P. Morgan on August 7 but was told it would not be invited, because of antitrust-timing risk. During mid-August to end-October J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants (three strategic, 24 financial); 15 financial buyers signed confidentiality and standstill agreements in the first week of October, received diligence and management presentations, and submitted one of six non-binding indications of interest due October 30. On November 3 the board advanced the four bidders at or above $80.00 to the final round; two of them combined as Bidder 3, which then valued the company at or below the market price and submitted nothing. Buyer Group bid $80.70 and Bidder 2 $80.35 on December 10; after the committee demanded improvement, their best-and-final bids on December 12 were $83.00 and $81.50, and the board approved the Buyer Group deal on December 13. The parties executed on December 14, 2014: $83.00 per share in cash, with Longview rolling 3,012,050 shares (~$250 million) into the buyer and no strategic acquirer reaching the final round.\"],\n ]\n for f in facts:\n     ws4.append(f)\n style_sheet(ws4, [32, 120])\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build.py (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/build.py\", \"oldString\": \" ['Account', \\\"\\\\\\\"PetSmart's board began reviewing alternatives in early 2014 and, after JANA Partners disclosed a 9.9% stake on July 3, 2014 and Longview publicly urged a sale, decided on August 13 to explore a sale and announced it on August 19. A private strategic suitor, Industry Participant, re-approached J.P. Morgan on August 7 but was told it would not be invited, because of antitrust-timing risk. During mid-August to end-October J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants (three strategic, 24 financial); 15 financial buyers signed confidentiality and standstill agreements in the first week of October, received diligence and management presentations, and submitted one of six non-binding indications of interest due October 30. On November 3 the board advanced the four bidders at or above $80.00 to the final round; two of them combined as Bidder 3, which then valued the company at or below the market price and submitted nothing. Buyer Group bid $80.70 and Bidder 2 $80.35 on December 10; after the committee demanded improvement, their best-and-final bids on December 12 were $83.00 and $81.50, and the board approved the Buyer Group deal on December 13. The parties executed on December 14, 2014: $83.00 per share in cash, with Longview rolling 3,012,050 shares (~$250 million) into the buyer and no strategic acquirer reaching the final round.\\\\\\\"\\\"],\", \"newString\": \" ['Account', \\\"PetSmart's board began reviewing alternatives in early 2014 and, after JANA Partners disclosed a 9.9% stake on July 3, 2014 and Longview publicly urged a sale, decided on August 13 to explore a sale and announced it on August 19. A private strategic suitor, Industry Participant, re-approached J.P. Morgan on August 7 but was told it would not be invited, because of antitrust-timing risk. During mid-August to end-October J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants (three strategic, 24 financial); 15 financial buyers signed confidentiality and standstill agreements in the first week of October, received diligence and management presentations, and submitted one of six non-binding indications of interest due October 30. On November 3 the board advanced the four bidders at or above $80.00 to the final round; two of them combined as Bidder 3, which then valued the company at or below the market price and submitted nothing. Buyer Group bid $80.70 and Bidder 2 $80.35 on December 10; after the committee demanded improvement, their best-and-final bids on December 12 were $83.00 and $81.50, and the board approved the Buyer Group deal on December 13. The parties executed on December 14, 2014: $83.00 per share in cash, with Longview rolling 3,012,050 shares (~$250 million) into the buyer and no strategic acquirer reaching the final round.\\\"],\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825509490,"end":1789825511580}}}}
