ned | 2 | None None | None None None | cnt None | ex None | flag Q1\n#24 | Dropped by target | 2 | None None | None None None | cnt 2 | ex Lower offer than rivals | flag None\n#25 | Bidding group changed | 2 | None None | None None None | cnt 2 | ex None | flag Q4\n#26 | Deadline set | 2 | None None | None None None | cnt None | ex None | flag None\n#27 | Bid | 2 | 80.7 80.7 | Yes Formal Light | cnt 1 | ex None | flag None\n#28 | Bid | 2 | 80.35 80.35 | Yes Formal Light | cnt 1 | ex None | flag None\n#29 | Did not submit | 2 | None None | None None None | cnt 2 | ex Value at or below market price | flag Q4\n#30 | Deadline | 2 | None None | None None None | cnt None | ex None | flag Q2\n#31 | Deadline revised | 2 | None None | None None None | cnt None | ex None | flag Q2\n#33 | Bid | 2 | 81.5 81.5 | Yes Formal Light | cnt 1 | ex None | flag None\n#34 | Bid | 2 | 82.5 82.5 | Yes Formal Light | cnt 1 | ex None | flag None\n#35 | Bid | 2 | 83 83 | Yes Formal Light | cnt 1 | ex None | flag None\n#36 | Deadline | 2 | None None | None None None | cnt None | ex None | flag Q2\n#40 | Not selected at signing | 2 | None None | None None None | cnt 1 | ex Lower offer than rivals | flag None\n\n#1 NOTE: Target's outside legal advisor; first seen acting at the June 18 board meeting and present at board and committee meetings through signing.\n   Q: At a meeting on June 18, 2014, the board reviewed, together with a financial advisor and with Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz (“Wachtell Lipton”), its legal advisor (21) (None)\n#2 NOTE: Disclosed 9.9% stake and intent to discuss alternatives including a sale; met the Company on 07/10/2014 advocating a sale; filed amendments and public letters through August 2014.\n   Q: JANA intended to engage in discussions with management and the board with respect to a review of strategic alternatives, including a sale of the Company (22) (None)\n#3 NOTE: Public letter urged the board to consider a sale and offered to roll part or all of its holdings into acquirer equity if needed; reiterated advocacy in a 07/10/2014 call with the Company.\n   Q: Longview made public a letter to the board in which Longview stated that the board should consider the a sale of the Company (22) (None)\n#4 NOTE: Financial advisor; retained in July after the Company interviewed several candidates; engagement letter effective 08/21/2014; served through signing.\n   Q: In July, after interviewing several potential financial advisors, the Company retained J.P. Morgan as financial advisor (22) (None)\n#5 NOTE: Approached J.P. Morgan about revisiting a combination if PetSmart pursued alternatives; no price; reported to the ad hoc committee; never admitted to the process.\n   Q: Industry Participant might be interested in re-visiting the conversations that had taken place in the Spring concerning the feasibility of a possible combination of the two Companies (22) (None)\n#6 NOTE: Board determined to explore strategic alternatives including a possible sale; authorized ad hoc committee oversight; planned J.P. Morgan outreach in late September–early October and a public announcement.\n   Q: determined to explore strategic alternatives (including a possible sale of the Company) for the Company to maximize value for stockholders (22) (None)\n#7 NOTE: Press release concurrent with second-quarter earnings announced exploration of strategic alternatives including a possible sale; interested parties could contact J.P. Morgan directly.\n   Q: the Company issued a press release announcing that it determined to explore strategic alternatives for the Company to maximize value for stockholders, including a possible sale of the Company (23) (None)\n#8 NOTE: Decided Industry Participant would not be invited into the exploratory process (antitrust concerns); communicated via J.P. Morgan calls 08/22 and 08/27; Industry Participant restated interest; no contact since.\n   Q: The J.P. Morgan representative stated that Industry Participant would not be invited into the exploratory process (23) (None)\n#9 NOTE: Inbound contacts to J.P. Morgan during process preparation; three strategic parties, not counting Industry Participant; no individual names or outcomes reported.\n   Q: including three strategic parties (not counting Industry Participant) and 24 financial participants (23) (None)\n#10 NOTE: Inbound contacts during process preparation; includes potential lead buyers and large suppliers of equity capital; the 15 October NDA signers are a subset.\n   Q: 24 financial participants (including potential lead buyers as well as large suppliers of equity capital to lead buyers) (23) (None)\n#11 NOTE: Process 1 round 1 opened as the Company began confidentiality/standstill agreements and October diligence; non-binding preliminary indications due 10/30.\n   Q: In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers (23) (Q1)\n#12 NOTE: Cohort of 15 financial buyers under confidentiality and standstill agreements; all received management presentations, detailed financials and Profit Improvement Plan information; no individual names given.\n   Q: all 15 of which, during the month of October engaged in due diligence, received management presentations involving the Company's senior-most management, and received detailed financial and business plan information (23) (None)\n#13 NOTE: Informed bidders that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due 10/30/2014.\n   Q: During October, the potential bidders were informed that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due on October 30, 2014 (23) (None)\n#14 NOTE: Told bidders Longview was willing to roll over up to 7.5 million shares on acceptable terms; bidders asked whether interested; participation not a condition.\n   Q: Longview had informed the Company that it would be willing to “roll-over” up to 7.5 million shares on terms and price acceptable to Longview (23) (None)\n#15 NOTE: Indication of interest; range $81.00–$83.00; one of three initial indications at or above $80.00; advanced 11/03; consideration form not stated.\n   Q: the Buyer Group, which indicated a range of $81.00 to $83.00 per share (24) (None)\n#16 NOTE: Indication of interest; range $80.00–$85.00; one of three initial indications at or above $80.00; advanced 11/03; consideration form not stated.\n   Q: another bidder, which suggested a range of $80.00 to $85.00 per share (24) (None)\n#17 NOTE: Identified as the third of the three initial indications at or above $80.00 after the Buyer Group and Unnamed financial bidder 1; price not stated; advanced 11/03.\n   Q: Three bidders initially indicated price ranges that reached at least $80.00 per share (24) (Q4)\n#18 NOTE: Initial indication of $78.00; raised after J.P. Morgan's 10/30–11/02 calls; advanced 11/03; bid again 12/10 and 12/12.\n   Q: another bidder (which we refer to as “Bidder 2”), which had initially indicated a price of $78.00 (24) (None)\n#19 NOTE: Residual of six 10/30 submitters after the Buyer Group, Bidder 2 and the two individually recorded unnamed indications; prices not stated; both below $80.00.\n   Q: six of the potentially interested parties submitted indications of interest (24) (Q3)\n#20 NOTE: Due date for preliminary indications; six submitted (rows #15–#19).\n   Q: non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due on October 30, 2014 (23) (Q2)\n#21 NOTE: 15 NDA signers − 6 submitters = 9; no submissions or reasons reported; closed at the due date.\n   Q: six of the potentially interested parties submitted indications of interest (24) (Q3)\n#22 NOTE: Raised from $78.00 to $81.00–$84.00 during J.P. Morgan's 10/30–11/02 rationale calls; helped qualify it for the final round; late relative to the 10/30 due date.\n   Q: increased its indication to a range of $81.00 to $84.00 per share (24) (Q2)\n#23 NOTE: Board advanced the four bidders at or above $80.00 to the final round; eliminated parties notified; November diligence, form merger agreement and FY2014 projection updates followed.\n   Q: determined to allow the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share to proceed to the final round of the sale process (24) (Q1)\n#24 NOTE: 6 submitters − 4 advanced = 2; indications below $80.00; notified by J.P. Morgan; none sought to remain above its respective initial indication.\n   Q: representatives of J.P. Morgan notified the eliminated parties, none of which indicated any interest or ability to remain in the process (24) (None)\n#25 NOTE: Two finalists permitted to work together and named Bidder 3 (one wanted an equity partner; one would drop out otherwise); members not identified (likely Unnamed financial bidders 1–2, see Q4); each leaves independent bidding.\n   Q: the ad hoc committee authorized these two bidders to work together. We refer to these two bidders together as “Bidder 3.” (24) (Q4)\n#26 NOTE: Ad hoc committee set the evening of 12/10 for final bids (later than the initial 12/05 plan, leaving 5 rather than 10 days before the targeted 12/15 completion, to cut leak risk).\n   Q: set the evening of Wednesday, December 10 (five days, rather than 10 days prior to the anticipated December 15 completion date) as the deadline for submission of final bids (25) (None)\n#27 NOTE: Final bid with revised merger agreement/documents; financing commitment documents provided 12/06; documentation less conditional and more favorable than Bidder 2's; not dependent on a Longview rollover.\n   Q: The Buyer Group offered $80.70 per share, in cash (25) (None)\n#28 NOTE: Final bid with revised merger agreement/documents; rollover accommodation would not affect price and only after a signed agreement; bid again 12/12.\n   Q: Bidder 2 offered $80.35 per share, in cash (25) (None)\n#29 NOTE: Verbal valuation not above ~$78 current stock price; J.P. Morgan called it unlikely to be competitive; no written offer submitted.\n   Q: Bidder 3 verbally communicated to J.P. Morgan that their valuation would not be above the current stock price of approximately $78 per share (25) (Q4)\n#30 NOTE: Final bids due; Buyer Group and Bidder 2 submitted; extended the same evening to 12/12.\n   Q: as the deadline for submission of final bids (25) (Q2)\n#31 NOTE: Same bidders asked to improve; new due date 12/12; an extension of the final round, not a new round.\n   Q: instructed J.P. Morgan to inform each bidder that it would need to increase its bid, and to instruct the bidders to submit improved bids on December 12, 2014 (25) (Q2)\n#32 NOTE: Approved Buyer Group's request to include a Longview rollover; Longview and Buyer Group signed a confidentiality agreement allowing exchange of detailed information, including bid price; voting-agreement form instructed.\n   Q: Longview and the Buyer Group entered into a confidentiality agreement permitting the exchange of detailed information between them, including bid price (26) (None)\n#33 NOTE: Best and final; revised merger agreement and financing commitment documents submitted; $81.50 confirmed as best and final.\n   Q: During the evening of December 12, 2014, Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash (26) (None)\n#34 NOTE: Oral offer; bidder working to increase within hours; increased to $83.00 same evening.\n   Q: The Buyer Group initially submitted an oral offer of $82.50 per share, in cash, but stated that it was working to increase the offer within the next few hours (26) (None)\n#35 NOTE: Best and final; revised drafts in substantially executable form; financing commitments provided; $250 million Longview rollover included.\n   Q: Later in the evening, the Buyer Group submitted a best and final offer of $83.00 per share, in cash (26) (None)\n#36 NOTE: Improved bids due; Bidder 2 $81.50 and Buyer Group $83.00 received; board acted the next day.\n   Q: instruct the bidders to submit improved bids on December 12, 2014 (25) (Q2)\n#37 NOTE: Board unanimously approved the merger with the Buyer Group and recommended adoption, subject to resolving remaining open points; J.P. Morgan oral fairness opinion; reconvene if needed.\n   Q: the board unanimously determined that the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger, were advisable and in the best interests of PetSmart and its stockholders (26) (None)\n#38 NOTE: Agreed price $83.00 per share cash; Longview rolls 3,012,050 shares (~$250 million) into Parent equity; equity commitments up to $1.83 billion and $6.95 billion debt financing.\n   Q: On December 14, 2014, the parties executed the merger agreement, the voting agreement and related transaction agreements (26) (None)\n#39 NOTE: Public announcement of the transaction on the signing date.\n   Q: issued a press release announcing the transaction (26) (None)\n#40 NOTE: Target chose Buyer Group; Bidder 2's $81.50 best and final was below the $83.00 winning price; still live at signing.\n   Q: neither of which was willing to make a definitive offer at a price above $81.50, which was lower than the $83.00 price offered by the Buyer Group (27) (None)\n#41 NOTE: First seen acting in the merger agreement notices; counsel to Parent/Merger Sub; exact retention date not shown.\n   Q: with a copy to: Simpson Thacher and Bartlett LLP (A-46) (None)\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"rows ok: 41\nsaved /home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/petsmart.xlsx\n#11 | Round opened | 1 | None None | None None None | cnt None | ex None | flag Q1\n#13 | Deadline set | 1 | None None | None None None | cnt None | ex None | flag None\n#15 | Bid | 1 | 81 83 | Not stated Informal Light | cnt 1 | ex None | flag None\n#16 | Bid | 1 | 80 85 | Not stated Informal Light | cnt 1 | ex None | flag None\n#17 | Bid | 1 | None None | Not stated Informal Light | cnt 1 | ex None | flag Q4\n#18 | Bid | 1 | 78 78 | Not 